A||N||5||Monkeyman||Info on Van Horn, TX||||5||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||11-17-2001||02:22 PM||||There is a very slight possibility that my wife may be offered a job in Van Horn, TX.  Anyone know anything about the area?  (Other than the fact that it's out in the middle of BFE?)  Is there anything around Van Horn (other than the Mexican border)?  Any info would be helpful.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/patriot.gif">    <BR><B><FONT COLOR="red">Proud</FONT> <FONT COLOR="white">to be an</FONT> <FONT COLOR="blue">American</FONT>!!</B>||||reg||5
Z||000001||maryjane||11-17-2001||02:45 PM||||Beautiful country. On I-10 in far West Texas. Mountainous area. About 50 miles as the crow flies to Mexico. A little further by road. It was however, in this area that led Gen Sherman to say "If I owned Texas and Hell, I'd live in hell and rent out Texas." Temp exceeds 105* several days a year. Things to do: Marfa lights- about 70 miles to the southeast. Davis Mountain State park/natl rec area/ about 95 miles away. Guadelupe Mtn Natl park 50 miles due north. What exactly do you want to know? My <BR>cousin's husband is from there and makes several trips back every year. Do you hunt? Great turkey and whitetail and mule deer hunting. If you go, learn some Spanish. I'll call my cousin-in-law & find out some more info. There is a forum member from El Paso, can't remember his username. He has a Fiero, a Vette (I think) & a trans am.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||11-17-2001||03:07 PM||||Any info is good.  Info specific to Van Horn would be great.  For example, are there any grocery stores in town?  How about entertainment?  (Stupid question.)  Etc.  I don't hunt so that's out, but there's got to be something to do out there.  It looks like my wife and I would have to make a special trip to El Paso every couple of weeks for anything other than milk and bread, but at least she could safely exercise her lead foot (is the interstate speed limit still 70?).  105* temps don't thrill me, but the knowledge that winter doesn't exist does.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  If you don't mind a quick long distance phone call, I'd appreciate any info you can get.  Does your cousin-in-law have email?  Would he mind trading some emails with me?  I don't remember much Spanish (took 4 years in HS, but that was 16 years ago), but there is plenty of software to correct that.  I have the boots.  All I need is a pick up truck and a big hat.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||maryjane||11-17-2001||03:59 PM||||Just talked to him. Population is about 2500.<BR>There are local grocery stores, but no chain type stores of any kind. Most people go to Pecos, about 90 miles to the North for shopping. There is a golf course, a newspaper. They claim the town is so healthy, they had to shoot someone to start a cemetery. But there is a hospital (25 bed). <BR>Van Horn Chamber of Commerce<BR>PO Box 762<BR>Van Horn, Tex 79855-0762<BR>Ph# 915-283-2043<P>Visitors Bureau<BR>915-283-2682 <A HREF="http://www.texasescapes.com/TOWNS/Van_Horn/Van_Horn_Texas.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.texasescapes.com/TOWNS/Van_Horn/Van_Horn_Texas.htm</A> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cheever3000||11-17-2001||09:37 PM||||That link didn't work for me, but any sites I found were, let's just say, "quick reading".<BR> <A HREF="http://www.iitexas.com/gpages/vanhorn.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.iitexas.com/gpages/vanhorn.htm</A> <P>and<BR> <A HREF="http://www.vanhorntx.com" TARGET=_blank>www.vanhorntx.com</A> <BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Cheever_gold_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||6
